ercent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.1.stable, 4.6.rc1\n- Not reproducible in: 3.6.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable unknown - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 11 Jan 2026 17:10:53 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Single-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (nvidia; 590.48.01) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13400F (16 threads) - 15.37 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nFog still affects the 3D scene when using the Display Unshaded mode.\n\nThis does not happen in Forward+ renderer. Fog is also disabled when using Display Unshaded in 3.x.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e041b31f-a570-4e4a-8b9b-75852828973b\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make sure you're using the Compatibility renderer\n2. Setup a 3D scene and enable fog for it\n3. In the 3D viewport menu, choose Display Unshaded: Fog still affects the scene when unshaded\n4. Switch to Forward+ renderer and check the difference: Fog does not affect the scene when unshaded\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test-4.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24658304/test-4.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rep